```ADD_PAPER
2508.13070v1
Reinforced Context Order Recovery (ReCOR) introduces an adaptive, reinforcement learning-based framework for extracting data‐dependent token generation orders in masked diffusion models. By self-supervising on token prediction statistics, the method dynamically evaluates the "hardness" of predicting unfilled tokens and selects the next token to unmask during both training and inference. Extensive experiments on challenging reasoning and planning benchmarks—including logic puzzles and complex text tasks—demonstrate that ReCOR can outperform oracle methods that rely on fixed or hand-annotated token orders. The paper provides thorough experimental analyses, showcasing improvements in accuracy and likelihood over both autoregressive models and traditional masked diffusion methods.
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
