^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ literature review ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
```ADD_PAPER
2502.03540v4
Path Planning for Masked Diffusion Model Sampling introduces a two-stage inference strategy that separates the token selection (planning) from the token refinement (denoising) process for masked diffusion models. The authors design "P2," an adaptive scheme where a planner dynamically identifies key tokens to update based on their prediction uncertainty, prior to applying a denoising step. This deliberate decomposition not only enables iterative correction of mistakes but also allows the model to focus computational resources on more challenging tokens. Extensive experiments across a diverse set of benchmarks—including math reasoning tasks and logic puzzles—demonstrate that P2 leads to significant improvements in accuracy and likelihood over traditional MDM inference strategies, making its performance competitive with, and in some cases superior to, autoregressive models. This work underscores the potential gains from adaptive token ordering by effectively balancing exploration (updating uncertain tokens) and exploitation (refining confidently predicted tokens).
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
