```ADD_PAPER
2510.04525v1
Demystifying MaskGIT Sampler and Beyond presents a novel adaptive token-ordering method for masked diffusion models by rethinking token selection in the sampling process. The paper introduces a "choose-then-sample" approach that leverages a partial caching mechanism along with a carefully balanced exploration-exploitation trade-off to dynamically select which tokens to unmask—thereby refining the generation process adaptively. Extensive experiments, including evaluations on text generation tasks and logic puzzles, are discussed in detail, showing considerable improvements in both accuracy and likelihood when compared to traditional autoregressive methods. The experimental results emphasize accelerated convergence and higher fidelity outputs, supporting the premise that carefully designed adaptive order strategies can significantly enhance the performance of MDMs against their autoregressive counterparts.
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
