```ADD_PAPER
2506.19935v1
Any-Order GPT as Masked Diffusion Model: Decoupling Formulation and Architecture reframes masked diffusion models within a decoder-only setting to disentangle the core effects of the diffusion paradigm from those due to architectural design. In doing so, the paper sets the stage for a principled comparison between adaptive token-ordering strategies in MDMs and traditional autoregressive approaches. It introduces an “any-order” objective that selectively prioritizes token recovery based on their intrinsic prediction difficulty and demonstrates, via extensive experiments on text generation and logic puzzle benchmarks, that such adaptive strategies can reduce inference time by a factor of approximately 25 while maintaining competitive perplexity. These experimental insights shed light on the potential of adaptive ordering to optimize accuracy and likelihood, thereby offering a robust framework for enhancing generative performance.
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
